#: src/implementation.md:1
msgid "Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:3
msgid ""
"The cache is a directory named `.justcache` alongside the `justfile` and "
"should not be committed to version control systems. It contains cache "
"entries named `HASH.json`, where `HASH` is the BLAKE3 hash of a serialized "
"cache key JSON object."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:8
msgid "The keys of the cache key object are:"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:10
msgid "`body`: evaluated recipe body"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:11
msgid "`environment`: map of environment variable names to values"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:12
msgid "`executor`: script interpreter or shebang"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:13
msgid "`extension`: script file extension"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:14
msgid "`extra`: user-supplied value"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:15
msgid "`inputs`: map of file paths to content hashs"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:16
msgid "`positional`: positional arguments"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:17
msgid "`recipe`: `::`\\-separated module path to invoked recipe"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:18
msgid "`working_directory`: current working directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:20
msgid "All keys other than `extra` and `inputs` are populated automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:22
msgid ""
"Cache key objects for invoked recipes can be printed to standard error with "
"`just -vv`."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:25
msgid ""
"The environment variables included in `environment` may be controlled with "
"`[cache(environment = EXPRESSION])`<sup>1.59.0<sup>."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:28
msgid ""
"The value of `extra` may be supplied with `[cache(extra = EXPRESSION)]`, "
"where `EXPRESSION` is an arbitrary expression evaluated with recipe "
"arguments in scope. Changes to the value of `extra` will cause a cache miss."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:32
msgid ""
"Before `just` runs a cached recipe, it creates a cache key, hashes it, and "
"looks for the corresponding cache entry."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:35
msgid "If the cache entry is non-empty, it skips the invocation."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:37
msgid ""
"If the cache entry does not exist or is empty, it runs the invocation and "
"writes `{}` to the cache entry."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:40
msgid ""
"File locks are taken on cache entries, so concurrent execution of cached "
"recipes by multiple `just` processes is safe. If two processes run a recipe "
"invocation with the same cache key, the first will take the lock, run the "
"recipe, write to the cache entry, and relinquish the lock. The second will "
"block until the first relinquishes the lock, see that the entry is non-"
"empty, and skip the invocation."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:47
msgid "The cache can be bypassed entirely with the `--no-cache` flag."
msgstr ""
